# What the build image must NOT receive.
#
# .env at the top of the list: it carries a DSN with a password. A Docker image gets pushed to a
# registry, and every layer stays readable by whoever pulls it — a secret copied in here is a secret
# published, even if a later layer deletes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local credentials, if any are lying around in the tree.
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key

# Useless to the build, and expensive to copy.
.git
.github
.claude
blueprint
docs
*.md
